Find all positive integers \( n \) for which there exists a sequence of positive real numbers \( a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_n \) that satisfy the following conditions simultaneously:
1. \( a_1 + a_2 + \cdots + a_n = n \);
2. \( a_1^3 + a_2^3 + \cdots + a_n^3 \leq \frac{n(n+1)}{2} \);
3. \( a_1^4 + a_2^4 + \cdots + a_n^4 \geq \frac{n(n+1)^2}{2} \).

To find all functions $f : \mathbb{R} \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ that satisfy
\begin{align*}
    f(x^{3}) + f(y^{3}) + 5f\left(\frac{z}{5}\right) &= 3f(x)f(y)f\left(\frac{z}{5}\right) \\
    3f(x)f(y)f(z) + 3f(x)f(y) &= f(x^{3} y^{3}) + f(x^{3} z^{3})
\end{align*}
for all $x,y,z \in \mathbb{R}$, does there exist a non-constant function $f(x) = cx + d$ for real numbers $c$ and $d$? If so, determine $c$ and $d$. If not, provide a counterexample.

